0ed69dd739b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700970} :answer-field/id #uuid "da4170bb-8109-559a-8085-bdde5c93bd88" :answer-field/key "value-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5ca0cd70-e4dd-5be1-a83f-c70573bd4bff" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=2x+2.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nEnter the four table values, then select the graph.\n\nFor $x=-3$, enter $y$: {{value-1}}.\n\nFor $x=-1$, enter $y$: {{value-2}}.\n\nFor $x=1$, enter $y$: {{value-3}}.\n\nFor $x=3$, enter $y$: {{value-4}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=2x+2.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=-3$ then $y=2(-3)+2=-4,$\n\n- if $x=-1$ then $y=2(-1)+2=0,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=2(1)+2=4,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=2(3)+2=8.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline y & -4 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/ae/aea0752d4e507c00063c2c5a8ede3a8cbe383de78ede9fc9a17a7218903477f9.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=2x+2.$\n\n![](images/84/840b1a33143718d3fdba042b36cbb29cc5864511cc4a5200c3fcc15821d72705.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94cb2f9d-a6ad-563c-ab01-985ef877f19c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uui