type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "93dc44e5-9c96-5aa2-8684-3f0562a4c471" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=-x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nEnter the four table values, then select the graph.\n\nFor $x=-3$, enter $y$: {{value-1}}.\n\nFor $x=-1$, enter $y$: {{value-2}}.\n\nFor $x=1$, enter $y$: {{value-3}}.\n\nFor $x=3$, enter $y$: {{value-4}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-x.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=-3$ then $y=-(-3)=3,$\n\n- if $x=-1$ then $y=-(-1)=1,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-(1)=-1,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-(3)=-3.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline y & 3 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/4c/4cba48e0ad715435a79ddeae81a38af2bfeba4d2f3ce2f57dbfa157ddebcfe5d.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-x.$\n\n![](images/b0/b01e5fd4b21edf3181d50d26e2929b481ec9cd93b8585ea475347483ce269655.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18434829-2739-5e3c-9771-46bc2caa0d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/72b26867ce21d5d5d2a1490dbea5283b10560275d4d9d50d5e3c8a9c0da09377.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700941} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a4338e-b4c0-55f3-8aac-d9acf3b75239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fc/fcafc484d6453441dbc3224dddf66659367991d9130df502d196568d204fd84f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700995} {:answer/id #uui