\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nEnter the four table values, then select the graph.\n\nFor $x=-3$, enter $y$: {{value-1}}.\n\nFor $x=-1$, enter $y$: {{value-2}}.\n\nFor $x=1$, enter $y$: {{value-3}}.\n\nFor $x=3$, enter $y$: {{value-4}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-x+3.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=-3$ then $y=-(-3)+3=6,$\n\n- if $x=-1$ then $y=-(-1)+3=4,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-(1)+3=2,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-(3)+3=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline y & 6 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/02/0221bc27b32d7a33b235c02cae9548973acaa6b8a6838d86422e52629c705713.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-x+3.$\n\n![](images/90/904dcf2cc1a58be2643dfaf5b00fa7d1ca0835a947d023082100b833537ad977.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701626 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff78d051-c055-568c-b88e-73371f1f3b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x - 6) (x + 8)}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff78d051-c055-568c-b88e-73371f1f3b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x - 6) (x + 8)}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701639} :answer-field/id #uuid "50a0827f-3bda-5080-8b28-f15f33d4c6f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24b7e1d9-33e3-586d-8b04-263308fb535a" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=2 t - 2,\\quad y=(t - 4) (t + 3),\\quad t\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation is\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}$,\\quad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.$" :question/worked-solution "Eliminate the parameter by using the $x$ equation to isolate $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x &=2 t - 2 \\\\ t &=\\frac{x}{2} + 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=\\frac{x}{2} + 1$ into the original $y$ expression, then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=((\\frac{x}{2} + 1) - 4) ((\\frac{x}{2} + 1) + 3) \\\\ &=(\\frac{x}{2} - 3) (\\frac{x}{2} + 4) \\\\ &=\\frac{(x - 6) (x + 8)}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe affine $x$ equation attains every real value, so $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nTherefore the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{(x - 6) (x + 8)}{4},\\quad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701627 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38f37859-031a-5098-ae5d-c733199939a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x (x - 5) (2 x - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38f37859-031a-5098-ae5d-c733199939a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x (x - 5) (2 x - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701629} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ff911f3-a432-53db-8399-216a90459a13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30b97f45-c700-5080-a3b3-045ca01ada91" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{2} - \\frac{t}{2},\\quad y=- (t - 4) (t^{2} - 25),\\quad t\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation is\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}$,\\quad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.$" :question/worked-solution "Eliminate the parameter by using the $x$ equation to isolate $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x &=\\frac{5}{2} - \\frac{t}{2} \\\\ t &=5 - 2 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=5 - 2 x$ into the original $y$ expression, then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=-(((5 - 2 x) - 4) ((5 - 2 x)^{2} - 25)) \\\\ &=- (1 - 2 x) ((5 - 2 x)^{2} - 25) \\\\ &=2 x (1 - 2 x) (10 - 2 x) \\\\ &=4 x (x - 5) (2 x - 1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe affine $x$ equation attains every real value, so $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nTherefore the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=4 x (x - 5) (2 x - 1),\\quad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701631 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20c220bb-6d24-5b9b-bc77-392bf4be691a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{(x + 3) (x + 9)}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20c220bb-6d24-5b9b-bc77-392bf4be691a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{(x + 3) (x + 9)}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701625} :answer-field/id #uuid "73f8b083-c6fa-58f8-8298-68131bfd2857" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4308e09c-0107-5fc5-9e53-e626f645f042" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=- 2 t - 5,\\quad y=- (t - 2) (t + 1),\\quad t\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation is\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}$,\\quad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.$" :question/worked-solution "Eliminate the parameter by using the $x$ equation to isolate $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x &=- 2 t - 5 \\\\ t &=- \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=- \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{5}{2}$ into the original $y$ expression, then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=-(((- \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{5}{2}) - 2) ((- \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{5}{2}) + 1)) \\\\ &=- (- \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{9}{2}) (- \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ &=- \\frac{(x + 3) (x + 9)}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe affine $x$ equation attains every real value, so $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nTherefore the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=- \\frac{(x + 3) (x + 9)}{4},\\quad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701636 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fde71e2-50e2-5916-a08a-e6178995d3a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x - 8) (x + 1)}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fde71e2-50e2-5916-a08a-e6178995d3a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x - 8) (x + 1)}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701630} :answer-field/id #uuid "325e1ef7-13ac-5892-9867-c0b1e9d8a71c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4785928-8dd2-50a0-aed4-1cce11289a1e" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=- 3 t - 1,\\quad y=t (t + 3),\\quad t\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation is\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}$,\\quad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.$" :question/worked-solution "Eliminate the parameter by using the $x$ equation to isolate $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x &=- 3 t - 1 \\\\ t &=- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{1}{3}$ into the original $y$ expression, then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=(- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{1}{3}) ((- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{1}{3}) + 3) \\\\ &=(\\frac{8}{3} - \\frac{x}{3}) (- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ &=\\frac{(x - 8) (x + 1)}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe affine $x$ equation attains every real value, so $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nTherefore the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{(x - 8) (x + 1)}{9},\\quad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701638 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb2f1cbb-77ff-5957-881d-18b2298d72dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 16 (x + 2) (x + 3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb2f1cbb-77ff-5957-881d-18b2298d72dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 16 (x + 2) (x + 3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701637} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4eb75b-8ff1-53b7-912a-223250c78bbb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3b850d2-763d-59b5-b973-fbaa4c4a4553" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{t}{2} - \\frac{5}{2},\\quad y=- (t + 1)^{2} (t^{2} - 1),\\quad t\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation is\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}$,\\quad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.$" :question/worked-solution "Eliminate the parameter by using the $x$ equation to isolate $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x &=\\frac{t}{2} - \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ t &=2 x + 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=2 x + 5$ into the original $y$ expression, then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=-(((2 x + 5) + 1)^{2} ((2 x + 5)^{2} - 1)) \\\\ &=- (2 x + 6)^{2} ((2 x + 5)^{2} - 1) \\\\ &=- (2 x + 4) (2 x + 6)^{3} \\\\ &=- 16 (x + 2) (x + 3)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe affine $x$ equation attains every real value, so $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nTherefore the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=- 16 (x + 2) (x + 3)^{3},\\quad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12cc82bb-1d6c-5fc7-9109-7e311933b3ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}x^2+\\left(y + 4\\right)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12cc82bb-1d6c-5fc7-9109-7e311933b3ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}x^2+\\left(y + 4\\right)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701969} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4670157-4e39-5aa7-a82b-c2842bca2b8a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5be06731-78c8-5f9e-b210-65cf942d30a5" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\sin t,\\qquad y=\\cos t-4,\\qquad t\\in[0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n{{field-1}}$=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx=2\\sin t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\sin t=\\frac{x}{2} \\\\\ny=\\cos t-4 & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\cos t=y + 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(y + 4\\right)^2 & =1 \\\\\n\\frac{1}{4}x^2+\\left(y + 4\\right)^2 & =1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe traced curve also satisfies $-2\\le x\\le 2,\\quad -5\\le y\\le -3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1769eb5b-dca8-5a62-860a-55273a7e8545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=\\frac{x^{2}}{36} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701970} {:answer/id #uuid "1a531641-d723-59d5-bd32-210b1a952514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=- \\frac{x^{2}}{36} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701971} {:answer/id #uuid "607eb96e-47eb-5c63-9d19-4f43e16c8b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=x^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701983} {:answer/id #uuid "a830915c-4a00-5eca-9077-9b5ad0c90ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=\\frac{x^{2}}{1296} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701989} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a45dbe-03e0-5f73-aa01-ddfc28f4074f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=\\frac{x^{2}}{6} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1769eb5b-dca8-5a62-860a-55273a7e8545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=\\frac{x^{2}}{36} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701970} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fe0c61c-64d2-5b3b-886e-1325fcd6ba91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "611b538a-4c91-5979-9392-db4acf86f88b" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=6\\cot t,\\qquad y=\\csc t,\\qquad 0<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx=6\\cot t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\cot t=\\frac{x}{6} \\\\\ny=\\csc t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\csc t=y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the Pythagorean identity $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$ by $\\sin^2 t$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sin^2 t}{\\sin^2 t}+\\frac{\\cos^2 t}{\\sin^2 t} & =\\frac{1}{\\sin^2 t} \\\\\n1+\\left(\\frac{\\cos t}{\\sin t}\\right)^2 & =\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sin t}\\right)^2 \\\\\n1+\\cot^2 t & =\\csc^2 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\cot t=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $\\csc t=y$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n1+\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)^2=y^2.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y^2=1+\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)^2.$\n\nExpanding the products or squaring the coordinate fractions gives\n\n$$\ny^{2}=\\frac{x^{2}}{36} + 1.\n$$\n\nThe traced curve also satisfies $x>0,\\quad y>1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701988 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48064f93-0307-5727-b1ac-9f7bfd4bd2b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{1+\\frac{x^2}{16}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48064f93-0307-5727-b1ac-9f7bfd4bd2b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{1+\\frac{x^2}{16}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701977} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c8912de-b87a-593a-8780-b11aa8d3d0fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e6becbe-0fc4-56e4-90cd-288b76135bf7" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4\\cot t,\\qquad y=5\\csc t,\\qquad 0<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx=4\\cot t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\cot t=\\frac{x}{4} \\\\\ny=5\\csc t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\csc t=\\frac{y}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity $\\csc^2 t=1+\\cot^2 t$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\csc^2 t & =1+\\cot^2 t \\\\\n\\frac{y^2}{25} & =1+\\frac{x^2}{16}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe used here that $\\csc t>0$ and $\\cot t>0$ in the range $0<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$\n\nNow, solving for $y$, we obtain\n\n$$\ny=5\\sqrt{1+\\frac{x^2}{16}}.\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=5\\sqrt{1+\\frac{x^2}{16}}.$\n\nThe traced curve also satisfies $x>0,\\quad y>5$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c826dad-f3bb-5c9a-9b0a-8e2e4ea74984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=\\frac{x^{2}}{36} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701976} {:answer/id #uuid "526c98b0-40ae-51bf-8c6d-5ea1eef9370f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=- \\frac{x^{2}}{36} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701980} {:answer/id #uuid "5deb5e99-bd0c-549f-98a3-581a45855fd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=\\frac{x^{2}}{6} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701982} {:answer/id #uuid "84a9efe1-d642-5b1d-8d1c-168396a8bf93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=36 x^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701986} {:answer/id #uuid "87307d58-97c5-5697-8f49-fd69eb024c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=\\frac{x^{2}}{6} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c826dad-f3bb-5c9a-9b0a-8e2e4ea74984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2}=\\frac{x^{2}}{36} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701976} :answer-field/id #uuid "801c6b30-ab12-5d26-9cb1-d1d4ef21feb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa43b2fc-04fc-5273-a02a-de2795bedcd3" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=6\\tan t,\\qquad y=\\sec t,\\qquad 0<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx=6\\tan t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\tan t=\\frac{x}{6} \\\\\ny=\\sec t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\sec t=y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the Pythagorean identity $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$ by $\\cos^2 t$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sin^2 t}{\\cos^2 t}+\\frac{\\cos^2 t}{\\cos^2 t} & =\\frac{1}{\\cos^2 t} \\\\\n\\left(\\frac{\\sin t}{\\cos t}\\right)^2+1 & =\\left(\\frac{1}{\\cos t}\\right)^2 \\\\\n\\tan^2 t+1 & =\\sec^2 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\tan t=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $\\sec t=y$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)^2+1=y^2.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y^2=\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)^2+1.$\n\nExpanding the products or squaring the coordinate fractions gives\n\n$$\ny^{2}=\\frac{x^{2}}{36} + 1.\n$$\n\nThe traced curve also satisfies $x>0,\\quad y>1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b149595-ca5c-5da2-aebc-9d8c2e4170a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(x + 3\\right)^{2}}{81} + \\frac{\\left(y + 2\\right)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701972} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd1e929-a964-5aaa-89f1-35db5572395f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(x + 3\\right)^{2} + \\frac{\\left(y + 2\\right)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701974} {:answer/id #uuid "3379e0db-0dcf-587c-83ba-59ae1601d058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(x + 3\\right)^{2} + \\left(y + 2\\right)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701975} {:answer/id #uuid "4a0d808e-f3ba-56a7-9f3d-a0f09e26bbd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(x + 3\\right)^{2}}{9} + \\frac{\\left(y + 2\\right)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701978} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c53426-6593-571a-a2fe-37747d2bd178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(x + 3\\right)^{2}}{9} + \\frac{\\left(y + 2\\right)^{2}}{81}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a0d808e-f3ba-56a7-9f3d-a0f09e26bbd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(x + 3\\right)^{2}}{9} + \\frac{\\left(y + 2\\right)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701978} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb135750-cdb4-543c-9e46-5946af59c508" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc5226ea-e549-5042-9532-bbf5fee71a22" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3\\cos t-3,\\qquad y=3\\sin t-2,\\qquad t\\in[0,2\\pi).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx=3\\cos t-3 & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\cos t=\\frac{x + 3}{3} \\\\\ny=3\\sin t-2 & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\sin t=\\frac{y + 2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{y + 2}{3}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{x + 3}{3}\\right)^2=1.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $\\left(\\frac{y + 2}{3}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{x + 3}{3}\\right)^2=1.$\n\nExpanding the products or squaring the coordinate fractions gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\left(x + 3\\right)^{2}}{9} + \\frac{\\left(y + 2\\right)^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nThe traced curve also satisfies $-6\\le x\\le 0,\\quad -5\\le y\\le 1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702823 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acf9a7a9-3585-5a8b-9eb2-e2cbca665b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acf9a7a9-3585-5a8b-9eb2-e2cbca665b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702847} :answer-field/id #uuid "5746e1fd-55b6-574e-b018-139fd4872a84" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32f6992e-0c21-524e-984c-5f63a19b250a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e0/e051781c50e50b674ae914596db04f75d261947d984ac6a30ac949e81b0b7810.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702817} {:answer/id #uuid "82c1eb81-14d2-54b0-a03b-08190be677f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/56fa91407fcfb9bea5168fd358fe666d8c73802ac5a3600c71ec799ceb43f454.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702834} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e56858-86fe-58e9-b69d-3a36c0a61e88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/74/74b82c2bf64943118f673451dff1dab2faeac01db913d4f4922f9db31b95025a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702844} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e7a361-923c-527f-83e6-373518187d18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/28/28f6a350350a65349d21f002018da5601397973639a8982e238eda4ab2099485.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702860} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc60620-42c6-5e7f-b469-f8cc016b65bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/45/455754194b8dec1c9d61d25e0ad5ff0e4f7dc8b723ac46db1c5336e9463338fc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82c1eb81-14d2-54b0-a03b-08190be677f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/56fa91407fcfb9bea5168fd358fe666d8c73802ac5a3600c71ec799ceb43f454.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702834} :answer-field/id #uuid "711474d9-6dd2-50ca-ab65-5d86292b9713" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dad3e0ba-a4c1-52ae-91ae-dd2da8d4b428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dad3e0ba-a4c1-52ae-91ae-dd2da8d4b428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702858} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd2623d-5443-51a9-a993-99579644661b" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48e56533-3638-5cef-86a2-4fe831144961" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=2+\\frac{1}{2}x$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-2$ and $x=4$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-2$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=4$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2+\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{2}(-2) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-2,1).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=4.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2+\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{2}(4) \\\\  & =2+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(4,4).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=2+\\frac{1}{2}x.$\n\n![](images/91/919fd8b9cae156ae75bd8c0767cbd82b7ee3cfbd99184e90bc22e991f6f9a310.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0195896c-7748-58d0-891a-8a093af2e601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/74/74b82c2bf64943118f673451dff1dab2faeac01db913d4f4922f9db31b95025a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702811} {:answer/id #uuid "45c9da0a-e8f6-5427-a340-5dadc3d23130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b3/b30edfb5a5e5e1e913c072ca609c81ab429f86c6eaa2be09b2e7e8e92016de8f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702822} {:answer/id #uuid "6fbad8e5-3aa1-509c-9e14-a843121985fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e0/e051781c50e50b674ae914596db04f75d261947d984ac6a30ac949e81b0b7810.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702831} {:answer/id #uuid "8d2ae9df-0a3d-542e-9451-d4390e12cb8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/28/28f6a350350a65349d21f002018da5601397973639a8982e238eda4ab2099485.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702837} {:answer/id #uuid "d971bc01-180a-5c91-88ae-e26086342f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/59d9e64dff92224c80fba287f60005a88f4193a131a8d32b7757e0b11a9f403f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0195896c-7748-58d0-891a-8a093af2e601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/74/74b82c2bf64943118f673451dff1dab2faeac01db913d4f4922f9db31b95025a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702811} :answer-field/id #uuid "2173a72c-6639-553e-82e8-73de05f2c34a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702814} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25288bea-312c-5d70-8077-b84697b45ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25288bea-312c-5d70-8077-b84697b45ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702815} :answer-field/id #uuid "a70a215a-9add-5a3d-9dcc-41ccb73f657a" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7afc84dd-83ca-5867-9327-952ae14f4cf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7afc84dd-83ca-5867-9327-952ae14f4cf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702833} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6e414e9-ca5c-5715-90f6-54976edc817f" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4db62e76-bdf9-5d4c-a9cd-8a17ee8d7c60" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=-2x+2$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-1$ and $x=2$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-1$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=2$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+2 \\\\  & =-2(-1)+2 \\\\  & =2+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-1,4).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+2 \\\\  & =-2(2)+2 \\\\  & =-4+2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(2,-2).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-2x+2.$\n\n![](images/3e/3e5a3637b65b6b08bfaeee49acdb9cd7e56002c33b2c6b4bfde654cddc456dbe.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9941a037-ad5d-5bd8-86a1-5b77545d1e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9941a037-ad5d-5bd8-86a1-5b77545d1e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702842} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4d91e10-74b7-5384-ad00-7980a10f52ee" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8688fb35-0552-5ce7-9da4-85408d32e4b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8688fb35-0552-5ce7-9da4-85408d32e4b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702835} :answer-field/id #uuid "d534e89f-e755-5651-9fb9-3137ba0d4524" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e6c2bbd-0b4b-5145-9a0f-cb2169f054a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f6c613ac31220b890d69fb2db001c126fb49d04621c3641d0848973db9954069.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702821} {:answer/id #uuid "6ae7e09b-4535-52ef-b7c7-3e728d6da930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/93/930ab140366898b219de63fd5acb6379891e39108eb4d4ea7a54ae4c2d4d558b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702830} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6347c5-ca4c-5490-833a-8b3324b2e203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bd63a41d04a0a3729537220f26466ac69802e90af04a08058c954b3a0ffcaae6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702848} {:answer/id #uuid "ee37cd07-0bf7-5190-ba83-4cd767f95f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8c353c411299420f50fef1bd9bbe6391b16dfe9cdbb61bf655becd41d8431df2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702862} {:answer/id #uuid "efcd9c2f-d673-55a8-acab-ac94177d00c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/091bc1230b8729d0468ad940937d64dd89b04ae25d82615c8225157e1d191d18.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb6347c5-ca4c-5490-833a-8b3324b2e203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bd63a41d04a0a3729537220f26466ac69802e90af04a08058c954b3a0ffcaae6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702848} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2d7370d-c4e5-5851-b930-74a5e52a1db9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "90a03fe4-52fc-5453-8c77-5a87bb021b25" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=x-1$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-2$ and $x=2$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-2$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=2$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x-1 \\\\  & =(-2)-1 \\\\  & =-2-1 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-2,-3).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x-1 \\\\  & =(2)-1 \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(2,1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=x-1.$\n\n![](images/ec/ec668c79a841a93bc51d38f54dd383dac2f7e18b3274e802e54bcfc4423c0732.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702846 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b7bc2c-5236-5a7b-b7a6-f6ff39c11fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/091bc1230b8729d0468ad940937d64dd89b04ae25d82615c8225157e1d191d18.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702812} {:answer/id #uuid "3614253f-1525-510f-a501-9df9eb6e03f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f6c613ac31220b890d69fb2db001c126fb49d04621c3641d0848973db9954069.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702819} {:answer/id #uuid "65cdf02a-4b8a-5adf-bb2f-5232723ece04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/93/930ab140366898b219de63fd5acb6379891e39108eb4d4ea7a54ae4c2d4d558b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 1