nt :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702859} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a6bf674-fe58-536b-952c-cdbe7df3af11" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ac4c6168-87b1-515d-bf6d-caeecf8aab15" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=- \\frac{1}{2}x-1$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-2$ and $x=4$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-2$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=4$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =- \\frac{1}{2}x-1 \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{2}(-2)-1 \\\\  & =1-1 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-2,0).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=4.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =- \\frac{1}{2}x-1 \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{2}(4)-1 \\\\  & =-2-1 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(4,-3).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=- \\frac{1}{2}x-1.$\n\n![](images/bb/bbbeb31e584377fd9a34457866ee85600a12199bc7d6df96e6613b6af2330f00.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31e69540-f6c7-56dc-987d-614895bb9d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8c353c411299420f50fef1bd9bbe6391b16dfe9cdbb61bf655becd41d8431df2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702816} {:answer/id #uuid "