iculty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "32e489c1-ede3-5d15-95b2-54f1444b6ab0" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=-1-x$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-2$ and $x=2$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-2$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=2$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1-x \\\\  & =-1-(-2) \\\\  & =-1+2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-2,1).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1-x \\\\  & =-1-(2) \\\\  & =-1-2 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(2,-3).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-1-x.$\n\n![](images/41/41cff7db12e9382e7d00e47ae475cd7117eb22afad7c815dcf88d89bfe26561e.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d78b5f72-6800-587f-bf85-46ad8657cc85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d78b5f72-6800-587f-bf85-46ad8657cc85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702947} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dac7f28-b3bc-5e36-bbd2-71aecb0216c3" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d54dd23-72