#edb/ref 17592186702934} :answer-field/id #uuid "60a56b4d-cd5f-5db6-a63f-d4791719e9b3" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db6d0cba-36f7-5354-801c-41d20a787ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db6d0cba-36f7-5354-801c-41d20a787ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702948} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d4593e8-dbfc-597d-9867-97139a774442" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c0e4fe61-f671-5ab1-90e6-fcf31f3bc33a" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=-2x$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-1$ and $x=2$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-1$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=2$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x \\\\  & =-2(-1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-1,2).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x \\\\  & =-2(2) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(2,-4).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-2x.$ \n\n![](images/51/512b9c0ce45238e9c1b7e6d12cfa828380311147037b8f8ba36b27cfa3c1320c.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e137a7-a5a7-5043-afa6-a5cec01df17f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\left(3 x + 3\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702953} {:answer/id #uuid "225eb47d-9398-525f-a617-0c5b6e26a915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\left(3 x + 3\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702954} {:answer/id #uuid "3a6a2067-d7ac-55c3-bc54-1ef3c431bd2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13 \\left(3 x + 3\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702958} {:answer/id #uuid "abb21755-1796-5a3a-a060-0ab4c77e1a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 \\left(3 x + 3\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702972} {:answer/id #uuid "c37f7efe-dc76-5c63-8d6e-c451c01cf72e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 \\left(3 x + 3\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "225eb47d-9398-525f-a617-0c5b6e26a915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\left(3 x + 3\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702954} :answer-field/id #uuid "887cb7d0-8b07-5431-9106-6c408adf8710" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27b02973-5d14-53fa-b0f3-0f20e21306bb" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\left(3 x + 3\\right)^{4}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$\n\nUse the decomposition $g(x)=3 x + 3$ and $F(u)=u^{4}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$. Recall that $f^{\\prime}(x)=F^{\\prime}(g(x))g^{\\prime}(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=3 x + 3$ and $F(g)=g^{4}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} F^{\\prime}(g)&=4 g^{3}, \\\\ g^{\\prime}(x)&=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(x)&=F^{\\prime}(g(x))\\cdot g^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ &=\\left(4 \\left(3 x + 3\\right)^{3}\\right)\\cdot\\left(3\\right) \\\\ &=12 \\left(3 x + 3\\right)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702968 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dd06ab6-3bac-5da4-aad5-d599405bf6af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702957} {:answer/id #uuid "a14e4f3a-6d71-50c6-b78f-8c10ad88ead2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702971} {:answer/id #uuid "ae2f84e9-dae0-58be-a7e9-61e48e61696e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 7 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702973} {:answer/id #uuid "e24881f2-b502-58cc-bff5-b141386c5261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 9 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702977} {:answer/id #uuid "fef08c3f-1a3d-5f17-a1aa-75d1330c52e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a14e4f3a-6d71-50c6-b78f-8c10ad88ead2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702971} :answer-field/id #uuid "84633511-a9fb-52a9-893e-04963af90c09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88e7d5b6-b471-539e-87fc-fa08afb6e2d6" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{3}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$\n\nUse the decomposition $g(x)=- 2 x - 2$ and $F(u)=u^{3}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$. Recall that $f^{\\prime}(x)=F^{\\prime}(g(x))g^{\\prime}(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=- 2 x - 2$ and $F(g)=g^{3}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} F^{\\prime}(g)&=3 g^{2}, \\\\ g^{\\prime}(x)&=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(x)&=F^{\\prime}(g(x))\\cdot g^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ &=\\left(3 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ &=- 6 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702969 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ea15979-dce6-5b9b-af29-e4eae6421075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\left(2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702952} {:answer/id #uuid "24e3e15f-4331-5357-ab77-2a966ba4c5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\left(2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702955} {:answer/id #uuid "698bffcb-587a-57c5-8412-175aa8279159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\left(2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702962} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba9456c-04bf-52de-ad1c-ce7756a00658" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\left(2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702965} {:answer/id #uuid "e0975ecb-7d5d-5e0b-9d55-3a99d01d212d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\left(2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ea15979-dce6-5b9b-af29-e4eae6421075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\left(2 x - 2\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702952} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e5cb8a0-3c79-506f-b278-6dcb81c0611e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93906bd9-c91c-5416-89b8-ac65ae4c1310" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\left(2 x - 2\\right)^{3}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$\n\nUse the decomposition $g(x)=2 x - 2$ and $F(u)=u^{3}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$. Recall that $f^{\\prime}(x)=F^{\\prime}(g(x))g^{\\prime}(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=2 x - 2$ and $F(g)=g^{3}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} F^{\\prime}(g)&=3 g^{2}, \\\\ g^{\\prime}(x)&=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(x)&=F^{\\prime}(g(x))\\cdot g^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ &=\\left(3 \\left(2 x - 2\\right)^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(2\\right) \\\\ &=6 \\left(2 x - 2\\right)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702970 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cfe12b5-2991-52b1-a11e-48b5772d7524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 10 \\left(2 - 3 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702951} {:answer/id #uuid "539dfe8c-e7b9-589b-a267-9e0006b859f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 \\left(2 - 3 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702961} {:answer/id #uuid "771df31a-cdb6-5085-8f16-dfe7635baa33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\left(2 - 3 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702963} {:answer/id #uuid "7974e9c2-9b0c-559b-bf52-c6d726303f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\left(2 - 3 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702964} {:answer/id #uuid "c9b42b2b-49bf-550b-8d83-554db39f46ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 9 \\left(2 - 3 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9b42b2b-49bf-550b-8d83-554db39f46ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 9 \\left(2 - 3 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702975} :answer-field/id #uuid "47aee049-326c-586a-8ab2-a92ea5268e6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97dd1eb7-ddec-5666-a5ee-e01dc5aa10ef" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\left(2 - 3 x\\right)^{3}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$\n\nUse the decomposition $g(x)=2 - 3 x$ and $F(u)=u^{3}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$. Recall that $f^{\\prime}(x)=F^{\\prime}(g(x))g^{\\prime}(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=2 - 3 x$ and $F(g)=g^{3}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} F^{\\prime}(g)&=3 g^{2}, \\\\ g^{\\prime}(x)&=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(x)&=F^{\\prime}(g(x))\\cdot g^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ &=\\left(3 \\left(2 - 3 x\\right)^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(-3\\right) \\\\ &=- 9 \\left(2 - 3 x\\right)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c5c9784-a171-5eca-85a9-ce67f5c07211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c5c9784-a171-5eca-85a9-ce67f5c07211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702989} :answer-field/id #uuid "2514be36-286f-5e28-be23-3fc50b07ba4d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702981} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a66a09ba-9ba7-59ef-a69a-1498df5e0361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a66a09ba-9ba7-59ef-a69a-1498df5e0361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702993} :answer-field/id #uuid "70611366-e99b-5d25-8d87-d25e5e57d5a0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2054a26b-60d2-588f-866f-34467e9a25b9" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle 2,0,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle 0,2,x\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=2 \\sqrt{5}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nUse the determinant setup\n\n$$\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\2&0&0\\\\0&2&x\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRecall that the magnitude of $\\langle u,v,w\\rangle$ is $\\sqrt{u^2+v^2+w^2}$.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values are $x=$ {{field-1}} and $x=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, compute each signed component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\2&0&0\\\\0&2&x\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\nc_1&=\\begin{vmatrix}0&0\\\\2&x\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((0)(x)-(0)(2))=0\\\\\nc_2&=-\\begin{vmatrix}2&0\\\\0&x\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=-((2)(x)-(0)(0))=- 2x\\\\\nc_3&=\\begin{vmatrix}2&0\\\\0&2\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((2)(2)-(0)(0))=4\\\\\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\langle 0,- 2x,4\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $N(x)$ be the sum of the squared components. Compute the magnitude, square both sides, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(x)&=(0)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(- 2x)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(4)^2\\\\\n&=4x^{2} + 16\\\\\n|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|&=\\sqrt{4x^{2} + 16}\\\\\n\\sqrt{4x^{2} + 16}&=2 \\sqrt{5}\\\\\n4x^{2} + 16&=20\\\\\n4x^2&=4\\\\\nx^2&=1\\\\\nx&=\\pm\\sqrt{1}\\\\\nx&=-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck each candidate in the squared magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(-1)&=20=20\\\\\nN(1)&=20=20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $N(x)$ is the sum of the squared cross-product components. Both magnitudes are nonnegative, so these checks also verify the original magnitude equation. In ascending order, all real solutions are $x=-1$ and $x=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32bdf88e-8c36-51c3-949a-8ce15cea994e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32bdf88e-8c36-51c3-949a-8ce15cea994e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702983} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd1288c7-ad15-5bbd-9d2a-6ef999d87ad4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a3980c-d576-5e67-9293-dca9b6a1fe2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36a3980c-d576-5e67-9293-dca9b6a1fe2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702984} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef66a9c7-9676-5b5f-89f5-5895757de043" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37df8885-1425-5d32-a412-3852eef8fb1e" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle 1,0,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle 0,x,-1\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=\\sqrt{2}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nUse the determinant setup\n\n$$\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\1&0&0\\\\0&x&-1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRecall that the magnitude of $\\langle u,v,w\\rangle$ is $\\sqrt{u^2+v^2+w^2}$.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values are $x=$ {{field-1}} and $x=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, compute each signed component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\1&0&0\\\\0&x&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\nc_1&=\\begin{vmatrix}0&0\\\\x&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((0)(-1)-(0)(x))=0\\\\\nc_2&=-\\begin{vmatrix}1&0\\\\0&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=-((1)(-1)-(0)(0))=1\\\\\nc_3&=\\begin{vmatrix}1&0\\\\0&x\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((1)(x)-(0)(0))=x\\\\\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\langle 0,1,x\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $N(x)$ be the sum of the squared components. Compute the magnitude, square both sides, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(x)&=(0)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(1)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(x)^2\\\\\n&=x^{2} + 1\\\\\n|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|&=\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}\\\\\n\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}&=\\sqrt{2}\\\\\nx^{2} + 1&=2\\\\\nx^2&=1\\\\\nx^2&=1\\\\\nx&=\\pm\\sqrt{1}\\\\\nx&=-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck each candidate in the squared magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(-1)&=2=2\\\\\nN(1)&=2=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $N(x)$ is the sum of the squared cross-product components. Both magnitudes are nonnegative, so these checks also verify the original magnitude equation. In ascending order, all real solutions are $x=-1$ and $x=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702988 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9fff91d-1177-506f-a01b-f1b5c228c508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9fff91d-1177-506f-a01b-f1b5c228c508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702996} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e51398e-1f1d-50d6-b757-4dcb2c672849" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f14423f-54d8-5f89-b34c-edc9233ab135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f14423f-54d8-5f89-b34c-edc9233ab135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702987} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9c503b8-2841-5632-b5ad-1ddd839880db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89d98fd5-c149-5858-badf-88d8242f6385" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle x,-1,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle 0,0,2\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=2 \\sqrt{2}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nUse the determinant setup\n\n$$\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\x&-1&0\\\\0&0&2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRecall that the magnitude of $\\langle u,v,w\\rangle$ is $\\sqrt{u^2+v^2+w^2}$.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values are $x=$ {{field-1}} and $x=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, compute each signed component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\x&-1&0\\\\0&0&2\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\nc_1&=\\begin{vmatrix}-1&0\\\\0&2\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((-1)(2)-(0)(0))=-2\\\\\nc_2&=-\\begin{vmatrix}x&0\\\\0&2\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=-((x)(2)-(0)(0))=- 2x\\\\\nc_3&=\\begin{vmatrix}x&-1\\\\0&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((x)(0)-(-1)(0))=0\\\\\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\langle -2,- 2x,0\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $N(x)$ be the sum of the squared components. Compute the magnitude, square both sides, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(x)&=(-2)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(- 2x)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(0)^2\\\\\n&=4x^{2} + 4\\\\\n|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|&=\\sqrt{4x^{2} + 4}\\\\\n\\sqrt{4x^{2} + 4}&=2 \\sqrt{2}\\\\\n4x^{2} + 4&=8\\\\\n4x^2&=4\\\\\nx^2&=1\\\\\nx&=\\pm\\sqrt{1}\\\\\nx&=-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck each candidate in the squared magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(-1)&=8=8\\\\\nN(1)&=8=8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $N(x)$ is the sum of the squared cross-product components. Both magnitudes are nonnegative, so these checks also verify the original magnitude equation. In ascending order, all real solutions are $x=-1$ and $x=1$."}]}
